@layout MainLayout
@page "/tools/online-clipboard"

<ToolsLanding Heading="Online clipboard — paste and share in one step"
              Description="Paste a screenshot or a block of text and get a shareable, auto-expiring link. No account, no install, end-to-end encrypted."
              Lede="Copy something on one machine, paste it here, open the link on the other. Nothing to install, nothing to sign up for."
              PasteHint="Paste anywhere on this page to start">
    <Body>
        <h2 class="db-h2">What it does</h2>
        <p>
            An online clipboard moves text and images between devices that do not share a
            clipboard — a work laptop and a personal phone, a remote desktop and the machine
            in front of you, a colleague on the other side of a chat window. Press Ctrl+V here
            and the content is uploaded, encrypted in your browser, and turned into a link you
            can send anywhere.
        </p>

        <h2 class="db-h2">Why this one</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Encrypted in the browser.</strong> The key lives in the link fragment and never reaches our servers.</li>
            <li><strong>It expires.</strong> Links auto-delete, so an old paste cannot leak months later.</li>
            <li><strong>Text reads inline.</strong> Small snippets render on the download page with a copy button — no file to open.</li>
            <li><strong>No account.</strong> Paste, copy the link, done.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="db-h2">Good for</h2>
        <p>
            Sending a stack trace to someone without mangling it in chat. Getting a screenshot
            off a locked-down work machine. Moving a config snippet, an SSH key you are about
            to rotate, or a wall of log output that a messaging app would truncate.
        </p>
    </Body>
</ToolsLanding>
